- How would you monitor and alert if privacy constraints are violated in synthetic data?

## Why This Is Asked
Tests the ability to reason about real-world flakiness in a simple worker, ensuring correctness under retries and duplicates.

## Key Concepts
- Idempotent processing
- Message deduplication
- Backoff and retry strategies
- Mocking external services for CI
- End-to-end vs unit tests

## Code Example
```javascript
// idempotent worker sketch
const seen = new Set();
function handle(msg) {
  if (seen.has(msg.id)) return {status:'skipped'};
  seen.add(msg.id);
  // simulate processing
  return {status:'done'};
}
```

## Follow-up Questions
- How would you simulate network/transient failures in CI to test backoff?
- How would you verify dedup behavior with multiple producers?

## Why This Is Asked
Tests end-to-end reliability of streaming reconciliation systems, focusing on critical aspects like idempotency, exactly-once semantics, drift detection, and rollback mechanisms under high throughput conditions—essential for fintech and large-scale payment systems.

## Key Concepts
- End-to-end testing in streaming pipelines
- Idempotent reconciliation and exactly-once semantics
- Drift detection and rollback/replay strategies
- Test data generation for duplicates and out-of-order events
- Performance validation at scale (1M events/sec)

## Code Example
```javascript
// Example: synthetic event generator with duplicates
function genEvents(n){
  const events=[];
  for(let i=0;i<n;i++){
    events.push({id: i, timestamp: Date.now(), amount: Math.random()*1000});
    if(Math.random()<0.1) events.push(events[events.length-1]); // 10% duplicates
  }
  return events.sort(() => Math.random()-0.5); // Shuffle for out-of-order
}
```

## Why This Is Asked

This checks ability to design a small-to-medium risk migrations, focusing on data integrity, rollback safety, and CI integration in a beginner-friendly but realistic setting.

## Key Concepts

- Data integrity during migration
- Migration rollback and idempotence
- End-to-end risk assessment with real-world flows
- Test data generation and diffing
- CI gating and feature flags

## Code Example

```javascript
// Migration test scaffold
async function testMigrationShadow() {
  const before = dumpOld("users");
  await runMigrationShadow();
  const after = dumpNew("settings");
  return compareSnapshots(before, after);
}
```

## Follow-up Questions

- How would you test partial migrations and ensure no partial writes remain?
- How would you handle nested/optional user settings during schema evolution?
